.SH NAME
CSSMathClamp \- CSSMathClamp
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSMathClamp\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed Object
Model API represents the CSS \f[CR]clamp()\f[R] function.
It inherits properties and methods from its parent
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathClamp()\f[R]
Creates a new \f[CR]CSSMathClamp\f[R] object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathClamp.lower\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] object containing the minimum
value.
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathClamp.value\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] object containing the preferred
value.
.TP
\f[B]CSSMathClamp.upper\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] object containing the upper value.
.SH STATIC METHODS
\f[I]The interface also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]The interface also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSMathValue\f[I].\f[R]
